  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 350 AM EDT Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nThe forecast area will remain in a northwest flow regime aloft \nthrough the bulk of the long term forecast period. Initially, a \nmore comfortable airmass characterized by 60s dewpoints will remain \nentrenched on Tuesday as a front remains stalled to the south across \nsouth Georgia/northern Florida. Moisture will gradually increase \nthrough midweek, and disturbances within the northwest flow will \nprovide some opportunity for showers and thunderstorms Tuesday and \nWednesday.\n\nBy Thursday into Friday, an additional cold front looks to push \nsoutheastward into the forecast area as a trough swings through the \nGreat Lakes. This frontal boundary and increasing moisture will \nprovide an impetus for PoPs to increase more markedly by Thursday \ninto Friday. \n\nTemperatures will remain largely close to normal with highs ranging \nfrom the upper 80s to lower 90s and fairly pleasant morning lows in \nthe 60s for much of north Georgia to lower 70s farther south.",
